3. NODE.JS SINGLE-THREADED?
---------------------------
Node.js ko commonly single-threaded kaha jata hai.

Correct meaning:
JavaScript code primarily ek main thread par execute hota hai.

Iska matlab ye nahi hai ki Node.js mein sirf ek thread hota hai.

Node.js background operations ke liye:
- libuv
- Thread Pool
- OS-level asynchronous mechanisms
- Worker Threads

ka use kar sakta hai.


4. V8 JAVASCRIPT ENGINE
-----------------------
V8 Google ka JavaScript engine hai.

Kaam:
JavaScript code ko execute karna.

Example:

const a = 10;
const b = 20;
console.log(a + b);

V8 JavaScript ko execute karega.

Remember:
V8 = JavaScript Execution Engine


