28. IMPORTANT INTERVIEW QUESTIONS
----------------------------------

Q1. Node.js kya hai?
A:
Node.js ek JavaScript runtime environment hai jo browser ke bahar JavaScript run karne deta hai.

Q2. V8 kya hai?
A:
V8 Google ka JavaScript engine hai jo JavaScript execute karta hai.

Q3. Node.js single-threaded hai?
A:
JavaScript execution primarily ek main thread par hota hai, lekin Node.js background operations ke liye libuv, thread pool, OS mechanisms aur worker threads ka use kar sakta hai.

Q4. Event Loop kya hai?
A:
Event Loop asynchronous callbacks ko coordinate karta hai aur ready callbacks ko JavaScript execution ke liye process karta hai.

Q5. libuv kya hai?
A:
libuv Node.js ko Event Loop, asynchronous I/O aur thread pool infrastructure provide karta hai.

Q6. Thread Pool kya hai?
A:
Thread Pool kuch operations ko background threads par perform karne ke liye use hota hai.

Q7. Non-blocking I/O kya hai?
A:
Jab Node.js I/O operation ke complete hone ka wait karke main JavaScript thread ko block nahi karta, use non-blocking I/O kehte hain.

Q8. setImmediate() kis phase se associated hai?
A:
Check phase.

Q9. setTimeout() kis phase se associated hai?
A:
Timers phase.

Q10. Worker Threads ka use kyun karte hain?
A:
CPU-intensive JavaScript work ko main thread se alag execute karne ke liye.


