30. ONE-LINE INTERVIEW ANSWER
-----------------------------
"Node.js is a JavaScript runtime built on Google's V8 engine. JavaScript runs primarily on a single main thread, while libuv provides the Event Loop and asynchronous I/O infrastructure. Some operations can use the thread pool, and CPU-intensive JavaScript can be moved to Worker Threads. This event-driven, non-blocking architecture makes Node.js efficient for I/O-bound and highly concurrent applications."


